import{_ as s,o,c as i,a2 as t}from"./chunks/framework.CqpfiAoK.js";const h=JSON.parse('{"title":"Entry 698 | Dual-Track Time Domain | Time Domain and the Multiverse-Realm Cross-Cosmos Time","description":"","frontmatter":{"title":"Entry 698 | Dual-Track Time Domain | Time Domain and the Multiverse-Realm Cross-Cosmos Time","no":698,"module":3,"tags":["Multiverse Realm","Cross-Cosmos Time","Dual-Track Time Domain","Cross-Plane","Time Synchronization"],"related":["14-Cultivation-Realm Unified Division","28-Cross-Plane Anchor Connection","697-Cosmos-Origin-Entity Time Dimension"]},"headers":[],"relativePath":"en/0698_模块3-双轨时间域-时间域与多元境的跨宇宙时间.md","filePath":"en/0698_模块3-双轨时间域-时间域与多元境的跨宇宙时间.md"}'),a={name:"en/0698_模块3-双轨时间域-时间域与多元境的跨宇宙时间.md"};function n(r,e,l,m,c,u){return o(),i("div",null,[...e[0]||(e[0]=[t('<h1 id="entry-698-dual-track-time-domain-time-domain-and-the-multiverse-realm-cross-cosmos-time" tabindex="-1">Entry 698 | Dual-Track Time Domain | Time Domain and the Multiverse-Realm Cross-Cosmos Time <a class="header-anchor" href="#entry-698-dual-track-time-domain-time-domain-and-the-multiverse-realm-cross-cosmos-time" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;Entry 698 | Dual-Track Time Domain | Time Domain and the Multiverse-Realm Cross-Cosmos Time&quot;">​</a></h1><blockquote><p>Module: Module 3 · Dual-Track Time Domain | Benchmark base: Documents 14, 28, 02 | Series: Dual-Track-Time-Domain Overview Deepening (Entry 27)</p></blockquote><h2 id="introduction-when-a-cultivator-simultaneously-lives-in-multiple-cosmoses-how-is-time-counted" tabindex="-1">Introduction: when a cultivator simultaneously lives in multiple cosmoses, how is time counted <a class="header-anchor" href="#introduction-when-a-cultivator-simultaneously-lives-in-multiple-cosmoses-how-is-time-counted" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;Introduction: when a cultivator simultaneously lives in multiple cosmoses, how is time counted&quot;">​</a></h2><p>The Multiverse Realm is an extended realm above Heng Yuan Zhou&#39;s nine realms (labeled &quot;pending Terminology-Committee calibration&quot;): the cultivator&#39;s consciousness and existence are no longer confined to a single cosmos, but may simultaneously span multiple cosmoses. This brings the dual-track time domain&#39;s most fundamental new question — how is cross-cosmos time synchronized? Each cosmos&#39;s time flow differs, each Cosmos-Origin Entity&#39;s time dimension differs, each planet consciousness&#39;s geological scale differs. When a cultivator simultaneously accelerates in Cosmos A, Quests in Cosmos B, and escorts in Cosmos C, how is his &quot;time&quot; counted? Six top-level axioms here form cross-cosmos-time rules: anti-predation axiom opposes cross-cosmos time predation; republican axiom of Myriad Races confirms Multiverse-Realm beings&#39; equality with ordinary beings; collective ascension axiom lets cross-cosmos operations serve Myriad Ranks; causal self-discipline axiom lets cross-cosmos time operations not disturb causality; law-first axiom lets cross-cosmos time rules stable. The universal equal infinite law: within the Anchor Symbiotic Civilization, all beings inherently possess basic infinite power; the easygoing retain a guaranteed basic infinity and will never be eliminated; strivers and Youth Supremes can superimpose more and higher levels of infinity. Infinite origin is inherent in all, so predation naturally loses its meaning. This entry focuses on the Multiverse-Realm cross-cosmos time.</p><h2 id="i-three-hard-problems-of-cross-cosmos-time" tabindex="-1">I. Three Hard Problems of Cross-Cosmos Time <a class="header-anchor" href="#i-three-hard-problems-of-cross-cosmos-time" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;I. Three Hard Problems of Cross-Cosmos Time&quot;">​</a></h2><h3 id="_1-1-flow-asynchrony-problem" tabindex="-1">1.1 Flow-Asynchrony Problem <a class="header-anchor" href="#_1-1-flow-asynchrony-problem" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;1.1 Flow-Asynchrony Problem&quot;">​</a></h3><p>Cosmos A&#39;s Origin Acceleration Domain flows at a hundred times external; Cosmos B at a thousand times external; Cosmos C has no acceleration domain. A Multiverse-Realm cultivator active in three cosmoses simultaneously — three cosmoses&#39; time flows are out of sync: he deduces a hundred years in Cosmos A, only ten years pass in Cosmos B, and a flash in Cosmos C. This asynchrony is not a problem, but the norm. The dual-track time domain&#39;s response: build a &quot;cross-cosmos time ledger&quot; for Multiverse-Realm cultivators — separately record his time experiences in each cosmos, not forcibly unify.</p><h3 id="_1-2-cross-cosmos-causality-problem" tabindex="-1">1.2 Cross-Cosmos Causality Problem <a class="header-anchor" href="#_1-2-cross-cosmos-causality-problem" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;1.2 Cross-Cosmos Causality Problem&quot;">​</a></h3><p>One time operation in Cosmos A may, through the cross-cosmos anchor connection (Document 28), ripple causality to Cosmos B. This cross-cosmos causal disturbance is the causal self-discipline axiom&#39;s most strictly constrained scenario. The dual-track time domain requires Multiverse-Realm cultivators&#39; cross-cosmos operations to pass the symbiotic court&#39;s cross-cosmos causal assessment (Entry 688) — ten times stricter than single-cosmos operation review.</p><h3 id="_1-3-identity-consistency-problem" tabindex="-1">1.3 Identity-Consistency Problem <a class="header-anchor" href="#_1-3-identity-consistency-problem" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;1.3 Identity-Consistency Problem&quot;">​</a></h3><p>A Multiverse-Realm cultivator may have different identities, different cultivation paths, different social roles in different cosmoses. How to guarantee that &quot;this cultivator accelerating in Cosmos A&quot; and &quot;that cultivator Questing in Cosmos B&quot; are the same person? The dual-track time domain&#39;s response: the Alaya Network builds a &quot;cross-cosmos identity anchor&quot; for each Multiverse-Realm cultivator — regardless of which cosmos he is in or what identity he uses, his core consciousness, civilizational weight, and causal records are uniformly managed by the anchor.</p><h2 id="ii-cross-cosmos-time-s-dual-track-adaptation" tabindex="-1">II. Cross-Cosmos Time&#39;s Dual-Track Adaptation <a class="header-anchor" href="#ii-cross-cosmos-time-s-dual-track-adaptation" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;II. Cross-Cosmos Time&#39;s Dual-Track Adaptation&quot;">​</a></h2><table tabindex="0"><thead><tr><th>Track</th><th>Cross-Cosmos Fit</th><th>Reason</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Origin Acceleration Domain</td><td>May parallelize across multiple cosmoses</td><td>Accelerated deduction has no cross-cosmos conflict</td></tr><tr><td>Quest Sediment Domain</td><td>Must single-cosmos depth</td><td>Questing requires immersion, no distraction</td></tr><tr><td>Cross-Cosmos Causal Review</td><td>Required</td><td>Prevent cross-cosmos disturbance</td></tr></tbody></table><p>Multiverse-Realm cultivators may simultaneously conduct accelerated deduction in multiple cosmoses, but Quest Sediment must choose one cosmos for deep immersion — otherwise Questing becomes &quot;sightseeing.&quot; This is the dual-track time domain&#39;s hard constraint on the Multiverse Realm.</p><h2 id="iii-cross-cosmos-time-and-myriad-rank-deliberation" tabindex="-1">III. Cross-Cosmos Time and Myriad-Rank Deliberation <a class="header-anchor" href="#iii-cross-cosmos-time-and-myriad-rank-deliberation" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;III. Cross-Cosmos Time and Myriad-Rank Deliberation&quot;">​</a></h2><p>Multiverse-Realm cultivators&#39; cross-cosmos activity involves multiple cosmoses&#39; Myriad-Rank interests. Therefore cross-cosmos time operations may not be unilaterally decided by the cultivator — they must be reported at the Myriad-Rank Council round table (Entry 669), supervised by representatives of each clan. This prevents Multiverse-Realm cultivators from using cross-cosmos identity to &quot;escape like a cicada shedding its shell&quot; — doing bad things in Cosmos A then running to Cosmos C to continue cultivating.</p><h2 id="iv-cross-cosmos-time-s-transition-to-the-balanced-anchor-hyper-multiverse-realm" tabindex="-1">IV. Cross-Cosmos Time&#39;s Transition to the Balanced Anchor Hyper-Multiverse Realm <a class="header-anchor" href="#iv-cross-cosmos-time-s-transition-to-the-balanced-anchor-hyper-multiverse-realm" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;IV. Cross-Cosmos Time&#39;s Transition to the Balanced Anchor Hyper-Multiverse Realm&quot;">​</a></h2><p>The Multiverse Realm&#39;s cross-cosmos time is the transition stage to the Balanced Anchor Hyper-Multiverse Realm&#39;s eternal time (Entry 699). In the Multiverse Realm, cross-cosmos time is still a &quot;multi-ledger&quot; — each cosmos records separately; at the Balanced Anchor Hyper-Multiverse Realm, all ledgers are unified into &quot;eternal time.&quot; This transition is not instantaneous, but the natural extension from Module Three to Module Four.</p><h2 id="v-five-core-takeaways" tabindex="-1">V. Five Core Takeaways <a class="header-anchor" href="#v-five-core-takeaways" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;V. Five Core Takeaways&quot;">​</a></h2><ul><li><strong>Anti-energy waste</strong>: cross-cosmos time ledgers keep Multiverse-Realm cultivators&#39; multi-line activity from chaos</li><li><strong>Anti-predation</strong>: cross-cosmos causal review strictly prevents cross-cosmos predation</li><li><strong>Tang-Luo upper-limit comparison</strong>: in the Tang-Luo system the protagonist&#39;s cross-cosmos activity is unsupervised; Heng Yuan Zhou&#39;s Multiverse-Realm cultivators are under cross-cosmos review</li><li><strong>Myriad Races full coverage</strong>: cross-cosmos operations are supervised by the Myriad-Rank Council</li><li><strong>Hyper-multiverse full openness</strong>: cross-cosmos ledgers, causal review, identity-anchor rules all public; newly merged cosmos automatically applies; may infinitely expand toward the Balanced Anchor Hyper-Multiverse Realm</li><li><strong>Axiom 6 · Universal Equal Infinite Law</strong>: all beings inherently possess basic infinite power; the easygoing retain a guaranteed basic infinity and will not be eliminated by the times; strivers and Youth Supremes can superimpose more and higher levels of infinity — infinite origin inherent in all; predation naturally loses its meaning</li></ul><h2 id="conclusion" tabindex="-1">Conclusion <a class="header-anchor" href="#conclusion" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;Conclusion&quot;">​</a></h2><p>The Multiverse Realm&#39;s cross-cosmos time is the dual-track time domain&#39;s key leap from &quot;single cosmos&quot; to &quot;multi-cosmos.&quot; Flow asynchrony, cross-cosmos causality, identity consistency — each hard problem has its solution. Cross-cosmos time is not a simple &quot;sum of multi-cosmos time,&quot; but an entirely new time-ledger system. It paves the road for the Balanced Anchor Hyper-Multiverse Realm&#39;s eternal time.</p><h2 id="related" tabindex="-1">Related <a class="header-anchor" href="#related" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;Related&quot;">​</a></h2><ul><li>Related documents: <a href="./697_模块3-双轨时间域-时间域与宇宙本源体的时间维度.html">Entry 697 · Cosmos-Origin-Entity Time Dimension</a> · <a href="./699_模块3-双轨时间域-时间域与衡锚超多元境的永恒时间.html">Entry 699 · Balanced-Anchor-Hyper-Multiverse-Realm Eternal Time</a> · <a href="./../wanling-hengmao-origin-universe-archive/docs/zh/28-跨位面锚点连接.html">Entry 28 · Cross-Plane Anchor Connection</a> · <a href="./../wanling-hengmao-origin-universe-archive/docs/zh/14-修炼境界统一划分.html">Entry 14 · Cultivation-Realm Unified Division</a></li></ul>',24)])])}const y=s(a,[["render",n]]);export{h as __pageData,y as default};
